  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity </title>
<para>Diego’s club earns money for charity when members of the club perform community service after school. For each student who does community service, the club earns $5. There are 12 students in the club.</para>
<para>The total dollar amount earned, \(E\), is a function of the number of members who perform community service, \(n\).</para>


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 5 a possible input value? Why or why not? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(n=5\) is possible. It means that 5 students perform community service.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Is 24 a possible output value? Why or why not? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>No, 24 is not possible as an output value. An output value has to be a multiple of 5.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Describe the domain of this function. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>All integers from 0 to 12</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Describe the range of this function. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Multiples of 5 from 0 to 60</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
